WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.217
Welcome to Module 2 of the
HR-Driven Identity learning path:

2
00:00:04.217 --> 00:00:06.938
run contractors from their own source.

3
00:00:06.938 --> 00:00:12.026
This is Gate 2, Sources, with
Chapter 02 of the developer workbook.

4
00:00:12.026 --> 00:00:15.281
In Module 1 you named one
writer for every account state,

5
00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:19.812
and saw that inbound provisioning writes
the leave date and the active value.

6
00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:24.212
This module applies that to the
people HR doesn't hold: contractors.

7
00:00:24.212 --> 00:00:28.328
You'll compute each contractor's
earliest end from several conditions,

8
00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.676
send the result through the
same middleware as employees,

9
00:00:31.676 --> 00:00:36.210
reconcile what the contractor register,
the card system and the directory say,

10
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.815
without changing anything,

11
00:00:37.815 --> 00:00:41.512
and write a sponsor review that
ends access when nobody answers.

12
00:00:41.512 --> 00:00:44.988
The code runs on fictional
contractors, on your laptop.

13
00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:50.350
It's illustrative: unit-tested against
fixtures, not run against a live tenant.
